---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import FAQ from '../components/FAQ.astro';
import ContactCTA from '../components/ContactCTA.astro';
import care from '../assets/care.png';
import { careFAQs } from '../data/site';
const steps = [
  { title: 'Begin with a clean vase', text: 'Wash the vase before arranging your flowers. Remove any leaves that would sit below the waterline; clean water stays happier without foliage in it.' },
  { title: 'Give the stems a fresh cut', text: 'Use clean floral shears to trim around 1–2cm from the stems at an angle. This gives the cut ends a fresh surface before they go back into water.' },
  { title: 'Add fresh water', text: 'Fill the vase with fresh water. If you have flower food, follow the packet instructions. Keep an eye on the level: a thirsty bouquet can use more water than you expect.' },
  { title: 'Find a cool, gentle spot', text: 'Keep the arrangement away from direct sunlight, radiators, and ripening fruit. A cooler room helps flowers last longer than a warm windowsill.' },
  { title: 'Refresh, tidy, and enjoy', text: 'Change the water every day or two, and trim the stems again when needed. Remove fading flowers as they tire, and give the remaining stems a little room to shine.' },
];
---
<Layout title="Flower care guide — Petal & Pine" description="Simple, practical tips for cut flowers: clean vases, fresh stem cuts, water changes, cool positions, and common flower-care questions." image={care}>
  <section class="inner-hero wrap"><div><p class="eyebrow">A little care goes a long way</p><h1>Keep the lovely<br /><em>a little longer.</em></h1><p class="page-lead">Your flowers do not need a complicated routine. A few small habits help each stem feel at home — and give you more time to enjoy the arrangement.</p><a class="text-link" href="#care-steps">The five little habits</a></div><div class="inner-hero-photo"><Image src={care} alt="Fresh flowers in clean water beside floral shears and an ivory linen cloth." widths={[640, 960]} sizes="(max-width: 760px) 92vw, 45vw" format="webp" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" /></div></section>
  <section id="care-steps" class="wrap section-space care-guide"><div class="care-guide-intro"><p class="eyebrow">From the first vase to the last stem</p><h2>Five little<br /><em>flower habits.</em></h2><p class="body-copy">Different flowers have different rhythms. These are general starting points for a mixed cut-flower bouquet.</p></div><ol class="care-steps">{steps.map((step, index) => <li><span class="step-number">0{index + 1}</span><div><h3>{step.title}</h3><p>{step.text}</p></div></li>)}</ol></section>
  <section class="soft-band"><div class="wrap section-space"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">A quick reminder</p><h2>Little checks.<br /><em>Lovely results.</em></h2></div></div><div class="care-table"><div><strong>When they arrive</strong><span>Clean vase, trimmed stems, fresh water.</span></div><div><strong>Each day</strong><span>Check the water level and remove tired petals or stems.</span></div><div><strong>Every day or two</strong><span>Change the water and refresh the cut ends.</span></div><div><strong>Whenever you move them</strong><span>Choose a cool spot, away from heat, direct sun, and fruit.</span></div></div></div></section>
  <section class="wrap section-space"><div class="section-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Every stem has its own character</p><h2>A note on a few <em>favourites.</em></h2></div></div><div class="three-up"><article><h3>Garden roses</h3><p>Soft outer petals can be part of a rose’s natural character. Give the stems fresh water and a cooler setting, and remove petals that have genuinely faded.</p></article><article><h3>Tulips</h3><p>Tulips can carry on growing in the vase and lean towards the light. Choose a vase that supports them and enjoy a little of that graceful movement.</p></article><article><h3>Mixed garden bunches</h3><p>Some stems will last longer than others. As the softer flowers fade, you can regroup the remaining blooms into a smaller vase for a fresh little arrangement.</p></article></div></section>
  <section class="wrap section-space faq-section"><div><p class="eyebrow">The little questions</p><h2>A few things<br /><em>you might wonder.</em></h2></div><FAQ items={careFAQs} /></section>
  <ContactCTA title="A little beauty for your everyday." text="Explore our flower palettes, find the mood you love, and put together a thoughtful brief for your next gesture." />
</Layout>
